import type { Lesson, Project } from '../../../types';

// Module 1: Welcome to the World of AI (days 1 to 4, no project). Written 2026-11-18.
// Facts checked on 2026-11-18: the term "artificial intelligence" comes from the 1955 proposal for the 1956 Dartmouth summer workshop (Wikipedia's page on
// the workshop; the proposal itself was not readable by the tools), ChatGPT's public release on 30 November 2022 (Wikipedia; openai.com refused the fetch),
// WHO's 2021 guidance on AI for health and its 2024 guidance on large multi-modal models (search summaries), FAO-hosted pages on phone apps that flag crop
// diseases from photos, UNESCO's 2023 guidance on generative AI in education. No product or version facts are stated, so there are no version notes.
// Every named app is described by the kind of thing it does and said to "commonly use" AI; nothing is claimed about how a company's own system works.

